  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q51-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "51",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=|x-2|$. Let $g(x)=\\dfrac{x}{2}-2$ for $x\\in[0,\\infty)$.\n\nFor what value(s) of $k$ will $y=f(x)+k$ and $y=g(x)$ have one point of intersection?",
